WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:03.000
-Welcome back to
"The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:05.167
It is time to play
a game of deception called

00:00:05.167 --> 00:00:07.000
"True Confessions."

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:09.000
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:00:15.567 --> 00:00:18.801
My first opponent tonight
is a Yankee legend

00:00:18.801 --> 00:00:22.167
and the founder and chairman of
the Turn 2 Foundation.

00:00:22.167 --> 00:00:24.367
Please welcome Derek Jeter!

00:00:24.367 --> 00:00:26.501
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:00:26.501 --> 00:00:28.467
Wow! You nailed that.

00:00:28.467 --> 00:00:30.467
You came right --
sliding right in.

00:00:30.467 --> 00:00:31.634
-Yes.

00:00:31.634 --> 00:00:34.067
-Derek and I will be
facing off against

00:00:34.067 --> 00:00:36.234
an incredibly
talented singer-songwriter,

00:00:36.234 --> 00:00:38.033
whose new single,
"You Only Love Me,"

00:00:38.033 --> 00:00:39.167
is out now.

00:00:39.167 --> 00:00:41.367
Please welcome Rita Ora!

00:00:41.367 --> 00:00:43.634
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:00:43.634 --> 00:00:47.934
-Oh, my gosh!
It is so good to see you both.

00:00:47.934 --> 00:00:49.033
Come on, now.

00:00:49.033 --> 00:00:50.300
That's exactly what
I'm talking about.

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:51.601
-This is great.

00:00:51.601 --> 00:00:53.601
-Before we start,
what's in the cup?

00:00:53.601 --> 00:00:54.868
-Alright, no, no, this is real
coffee in the cup.

00:00:54.868 --> 00:00:56.000
Yeah, here we go.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:57.167
This is like
a real old-timey detective.

00:00:57.167 --> 00:00:58.634
-Oh it is.
It smells like coffee, too.

00:00:58.634 --> 00:00:59.767
-Yeah, I wouldn't --
No, don't drink it.

00:00:59.767 --> 00:01:01.000
-Okay, okay. Sorry.
-It's not really coffee.

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:02.200
Alright, here's how this works.

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:03.300
In front of each of us

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:05.267
are two envelopes
containing confessions.

00:01:05.267 --> 00:01:07.334
One is true. The other is a lie.

00:01:07.334 --> 00:01:08.567
Once you read your confession,

00:01:08.567 --> 00:01:10.901
the other two players
get to interrogate you.

00:01:10.901 --> 00:01:12.868
Then you have to come to
a unanimous decision --

00:01:12.868 --> 00:01:15.133
is it the truth or is it a lie?

00:01:15.133 --> 00:01:17.701
-Why is the only song
in my head right now

00:01:17.701 --> 00:01:19.567
that should
suit this segment is...

00:01:19.567 --> 00:01:21.100
♪ These are my confessions ♪

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:22.934
♪ Just when I thought I said ♪

00:01:22.934 --> 00:01:24.367
I feel like you should do that.
-I should do that?

00:01:24.367 --> 00:01:25.567
-Yeah.

00:01:25.567 --> 00:01:27.501
-You've gotta teach me
how to sing and dance.

00:01:27.501 --> 00:01:29.767
Okay, here we go.
-ADHD, ADHD.

00:01:29.767 --> 00:01:31.601
-I think, Derek,
you go first, okay?

00:01:31.601 --> 00:01:32.968
Which envelope should he open?
1 or 2?

00:01:32.968 --> 00:01:36.234
-Pick 2!

00:01:36.234 --> 00:01:38.467
-Of course, everyone's -- Wow,
I didn't even think about that.

00:01:38.467 --> 00:01:39.834
-Yeah.
-Yeah. Number 2, yeah.

00:01:39.834 --> 00:01:42.200
-Do you have anything stronger
than that coffee?

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:45.100
-Really, okay, here we go.
-Oh.

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:53.968
-You're Derek Jeter.
-Yeah.

00:01:53.968 --> 00:01:55.434
-We would have known.

00:01:55.434 --> 00:01:57.834
-But I'm sure you have, like,
a really well-sculpted bottom.

00:01:57.834 --> 00:01:59.167
Do you know what I mean?

00:01:59.167 --> 00:02:01.801
-Were you talking to me or you
were looking at Derek?

00:02:01.801 --> 00:02:03.667
-Sorry. I meant you.
-Thank you.

00:02:03.667 --> 00:02:04.801
-Alright.
-Wait, what --

00:02:04.801 --> 00:02:07.033
-Is that a question?
-Thousands -- Where?

00:02:07.033 --> 00:02:08.868
Where were there
thousands of people?

00:02:08.868 --> 00:02:11.200
-In New York.
-Yeah, in New York.

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:12.634
-Yes.

00:02:12.634 --> 00:02:16.267
-Were you wearing the thong
where one would wear a thong?

00:02:16.267 --> 00:02:18.801
-Where else would you
wear a thong?

00:02:18.801 --> 00:02:20.601
-I don't know,
but I thought maybe, like,

00:02:20.601 --> 00:02:22.100
it was a weird trick question
or something.

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:24.300
-I wore it where
one would wear a thong, yes.

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:26.400
-So, do you wear underwear?

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:27.501
-Ooh!

00:02:27.501 --> 00:02:28.901
-I do.
-In general.

00:02:28.901 --> 00:02:30.067
-I do.
-Okay.

00:02:30.067 --> 00:02:31.601
So you've never gone, like --
-Obviously.

00:02:31.601 --> 00:02:34.167
-You have your own line of
underwear, don't you?

00:02:34.167 --> 00:02:35.300
Athletic wear.

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:36.501
-Athletic, yeah.

00:02:36.501 --> 00:02:39.300
-But these weren't your --
Was it your thong?

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:43.868
-No, it was not my thong.

00:02:43.868 --> 00:02:45.234
-Wow!
-It was not my thong.

00:02:45.234 --> 00:02:47.567
-It was not your thong.
Did you have anything else on?

00:02:47.567 --> 00:02:49.200
-I don't believe him.
I don't believe him.

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:51.400
-Did you have anything else on?

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:53.634
-I did.
-So, now we pick, right?

00:02:53.634 --> 00:02:54.701
We choose, we decide.
-Yeah, what do you think?

00:02:54.701 --> 00:02:57.067
I say --
-I say no. I say lie.

00:02:57.067 --> 00:02:59.234
-I say lie.
[ Drumroll ]

00:02:59.234 --> 00:03:01.534
-It is the truth.

00:03:01.534 --> 00:03:03.467
-Wait.
What are you talking about?

00:03:03.467 --> 00:03:05.033
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:03:05.033 --> 00:03:09.133
What?! How did...
What are you talking about?

00:03:09.133 --> 00:03:11.968
-Hold on, hold on. Hold --
Wait wait, wait.

00:03:11.968 --> 00:03:13.434
-What in the world?
-Let me see.

00:03:13.434 --> 00:03:15.634
-I'm going to ultimately
regret playing this game,

00:03:15.634 --> 00:03:17.501
but let me explain.

00:03:17.501 --> 00:03:18.767
-Please.
-Let me explain shortly.

00:03:18.767 --> 00:03:22.334
I had a new teammate
that I played with in 2002,

00:03:22.334 --> 00:03:25.067
and he always had a gold thong
hanging from his locker.

00:03:25.067 --> 00:03:27.367
And he told me,
"Anytime you struggle,

00:03:27.367 --> 00:03:30.367
you wear the gold thong,
you're guaranteed to get a hit."

00:03:30.367 --> 00:03:31.901
Now, I thought the guy
was crazy.

00:03:31.901 --> 00:03:33.701
So, in 2004, I went through

00:03:33.701 --> 00:03:36.067
the worst offensive stretch
in my career.

00:03:36.067 --> 00:03:37.334
-Okay.

00:03:37.334 --> 00:03:41.734
-And every day, I'd walk in,
he'd point at the thong.

00:03:41.734 --> 00:03:46.300
So, finally, I wore the thong.
Now, it wasn't thong-to-skin.

00:03:46.300 --> 00:03:47.834
I had shorts on underneath.

00:03:47.834 --> 00:03:49.701
So I put the thong
over the shorts.

00:03:49.701 --> 00:03:52.267
First pitch, home run.
-Oh, my gosh!

00:03:52.267 --> 00:03:53.901
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yes, yes.

00:03:53.901 --> 00:03:55.033
-No way.
-That is true.

00:03:55.033 --> 00:03:57.267
-The golden thong.
-Yes.

00:03:57.267 --> 00:03:58.801
-Wow!
I can't believe that's real.

00:03:58.801 --> 00:04:01.534
Okay. Alright.
Which envelope should I open?

00:04:01.534 --> 00:04:02.868
-Ooh, yeah.
-1 or 2?

00:04:02.868 --> 00:04:04.534
[ Indistinct shouting ]

00:04:04.534 --> 00:04:07.267
That's interesting.
I was hoping for 2, maybe.

00:04:07.267 --> 00:04:09.100
Well, I don't even know
what they are.

00:04:10.834 --> 00:04:12.801
[ Chuckles ]

00:04:12.801 --> 00:04:14.567
-Why are you looking at me?
-I'm just laughing.

00:04:14.567 --> 00:04:16.100
-Oh, okay.

00:04:23.033 --> 00:04:25.334
-Where was this concert?

00:04:25.334 --> 00:04:27.400
-It was in New Jersey.
-Indoor or outdoor?

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:28.601
-Outdoor.

00:04:28.601 --> 00:04:32.667
-What era of
Red Hot Chili Peppers was this?

00:04:32.667 --> 00:04:33.667
-Foo fighters opened for them.

00:04:33.667 --> 00:04:36.234
-Oh. Oh!
-It was a great concert.

00:04:36.234 --> 00:04:38.901
-Okay.
-I'd say 2000-something.

00:04:38.901 --> 00:04:41.434
-What time of the year?
-This was summer.

00:04:41.434 --> 00:04:44.300
-But Anthony never wears,
really, a top himself.

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:45.434
-That's true.

00:04:45.434 --> 00:04:48.667
-So why would you
give him a top?

00:04:48.667 --> 00:04:51.901
-He liked my shirt.
-Mm.

00:04:51.901 --> 00:04:53.634
-And where did he put it?

00:04:53.634 --> 00:04:56.834
-Wore it as a shirt.

00:04:56.834 --> 00:04:59.167
-Where were you sitting?

00:04:59.167 --> 00:05:01.067
-That's a good question.

00:05:01.067 --> 00:05:02.968
I was on the side of the stage.

00:05:02.968 --> 00:05:04.267
-Obviously.

00:05:04.267 --> 00:05:05.534
-Well, I was on the side
of the stage.

00:05:05.534 --> 00:05:06.934
I was talking to them.

00:05:06.934 --> 00:05:09.868
He saw my shirt, wanted it,
said "I like your shirt,

00:05:09.868 --> 00:05:11.367
I want that,"
or something like that,

00:05:11.367 --> 00:05:13.868
and then, like, gestured to me
to give it to him or something.

00:05:13.868 --> 00:05:15.767
-I don't believe it.
-What color was the shirt?

00:05:15.767 --> 00:05:18.000
-It was a white T-shirt.
-Too many words.

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:20.267
You're using too many words.

00:05:20.267 --> 00:05:22.501
-Sometimes, I use too many --
I'm a talk-show host.

00:05:22.501 --> 00:05:23.801
-And I'm a huge --
[ Laughter ]

00:05:23.801 --> 00:05:27.234
And I'm a huge
Red Hot Chili Peppers fan

00:05:27.234 --> 00:05:31.801
and I love how focused Anthony
is onstage when he sings.

00:05:31.801 --> 00:05:33.567
He's not going to notice you
on the side of stage.

00:05:33.567 --> 00:05:35.367
-Oh, wow. I think, yeah --

00:05:35.367 --> 00:05:37.167
-No, not in that way.
Not in that way.

00:05:37.167 --> 00:05:38.567
No, no, no.

00:05:38.567 --> 00:05:41.868
-I'm gonna say true
just so you got noticed. Yes.

00:05:41.868 --> 00:05:43.834
-You're worried about my ego.

00:05:43.834 --> 00:05:45.801
But here's the thing.
I took off my shirt.

00:05:45.801 --> 00:05:47.601
He was not wearing a shirt.

00:05:47.601 --> 00:05:49.667
So I thought, "Well,
I'll give him the shirt,

00:05:49.667 --> 00:05:51.367
but he'll give me
something to wear back."

00:05:51.367 --> 00:05:53.501
And he gave me nothing back.

00:05:53.501 --> 00:05:55.234
So I'm standing there shirtless.

00:05:55.234 --> 00:05:57.167
And I --
You know me a little bit.

00:05:57.167 --> 00:05:58.968
I don't want to be
shirtless in public.

00:05:58.968 --> 00:06:00.534
-You are talking too much now.
-What do you think?

00:06:00.534 --> 00:06:03.601
You're talking way too much now.
I say it's not true.

00:06:03.601 --> 00:06:05.534
-Yeah, me too. Yeah.

00:06:05.534 --> 00:06:08.300
-You got me.
It's not true at all.

00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:09.601
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:06:09.601 --> 00:06:12.601
-Talking too much.
-Yes.

00:06:12.601 --> 00:06:15.033
-I was talking too much.
-You were talking way too much.

00:06:15.033 --> 00:06:17.033
-I was talking way too much.
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:06:17.033 --> 00:06:18.968
-I planned the story out
all day,

00:06:18.968 --> 00:06:21.300
this fake story,
and I just failed massively.

00:06:21.300 --> 00:06:23.501
-Failed.
-Oh, I'm embarrassed.

00:06:23.501 --> 00:06:25.634
Oh, my gosh.
You totally busted me.

00:06:25.634 --> 00:06:27.200
Oh, my gosh.
It didn't happen at all.

00:06:27.200 --> 00:06:29.167
Alright, alright.
Rita, it's now your turn.

00:06:29.167 --> 00:06:30.367
Which envelope?
What do you think?

00:06:30.367 --> 00:06:32.601
-What do you guys --
[ Indistinct shouting ]

00:06:32.601 --> 00:06:34.100
-You totally busted me.

00:06:34.100 --> 00:06:35.234
-1?

00:06:35.234 --> 00:06:37.334
2? 2?

00:06:37.334 --> 00:06:38.801
2. I can't hear. Can you --

00:06:38.801 --> 00:06:40.033
-Someone's yelling "4."

00:06:40.033 --> 00:06:41.801
so it doesn't even matter
at this point.

00:06:41.801 --> 00:06:44.200
-I'm gonna go with 2.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:47.567 --> 00:06:50.701
-[ Laughs ]

00:06:50.701 --> 00:06:52.767
This one seems good.

00:06:59.133 --> 00:07:01.100
♪♪

00:07:01.100 --> 00:07:02.701
-Where was this?

00:07:02.701 --> 00:07:05.434
-In New York City.
-Okay.

00:07:05.434 --> 00:07:06.834
-I don't know
what accent that was.

00:07:06.834 --> 00:07:08.467
-Yeah, it was like
a Southern accent, yeah.

00:07:08.467 --> 00:07:10.601
But New York -- So, paparazzi --

00:07:10.601 --> 00:07:12.300
Normally, you're running away
from paparazzi.

00:07:12.300 --> 00:07:14.601
You went the other way
and said, "Let's be friends,

00:07:14.601 --> 00:07:16.000
