00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:19.400
-Well, it wasn't
a friendly exchange,

00:07:19.400 --> 00:07:21.734
but it was a savior exchange.

00:07:21.734 --> 00:07:25.567
I was being saved.
-Were you by yourself?

00:07:25.567 --> 00:07:30.100
-No, I was with my driver,
driving me to the airport.

00:07:30.100 --> 00:07:31.634
-I'm sorry.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:07:31.634 --> 00:07:32.801
-Yeah, so you're with
your driver,

00:07:32.801 --> 00:07:34.234
then the paparazzi
drove you to the airport?

00:07:34.234 --> 00:07:36.467
-Hold on.
-Did they drive your car?

00:07:36.467 --> 00:07:37.701
-That's interesting.
So there's two cars?

00:07:37.701 --> 00:07:38.801
-No.

00:07:38.801 --> 00:07:40.400
-Were you, like,
Jean-Claude Van Damme-ing,

00:07:40.400 --> 00:07:43.234
two legs on both cars, cruising
through on your way to --

00:07:43.234 --> 00:07:46.334
-Guys, guys --
-Where did you jump in the car?

00:07:46.334 --> 00:07:47.534
-On the street.

00:07:47.534 --> 00:07:50.300
-Yeah, in the city or --
-Like, on the motorway.

00:07:50.300 --> 00:07:52.467
Highway. Highway.
-On the highway.

00:07:52.467 --> 00:07:53.467
So you pulled over
on the highway

00:07:53.467 --> 00:07:55.234
and then jumped in the car.

00:07:55.234 --> 00:07:57.100
-And paparazzi pulled --
And you --

00:07:57.100 --> 00:07:58.133
-And the paparazzi
pulled up behind me.

00:07:58.133 --> 00:08:00.434
-You thought
you were safe enough

00:08:00.434 --> 00:08:02.033
to get in the car
with paparazzi strangers?

00:08:02.033 --> 00:08:03.400
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:08:03.400 --> 00:08:05.100
-If any kid's watching at home,
never do this.

00:08:05.100 --> 00:08:06.667
-No.

00:08:06.667 --> 00:08:12.234
No, but this was
a really serious emergency.

00:08:12.234 --> 00:08:13.400
-I hope I'm right.
-This was an emergency.

00:08:13.400 --> 00:08:14.467
-What do you think?
-I hope I'm right.

00:08:14.467 --> 00:08:16.033
-Okay, what?
-Yeah, me too. Yeah.

00:08:16.033 --> 00:08:17.701
-I don't believe it.
-I don't believe it at all.

00:08:17.701 --> 00:08:20.267
You would never, Rita Ora,
ever in your life,

00:08:20.267 --> 00:08:22.701
ever risk -- You are a treasure.

00:08:22.701 --> 00:08:24.834
You cannot risk getting in
a car with a stranger

00:08:24.834 --> 00:08:26.534
ever in your life.

00:08:26.534 --> 00:08:28.100
Is it true?

00:08:28.100 --> 00:08:30.000
-It's true.
-Oh, my gosh!

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:31.734
Rita, no!

00:08:31.734 --> 00:08:33.567
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:08:33.567 --> 00:08:35.734
Were you scared? When was this?

00:08:35.734 --> 00:08:38.300
-Explain.
-So, my car broke down.

00:08:38.300 --> 00:08:40.968
And I had to catch this flight.

00:08:40.968 --> 00:08:43.834
Like, I had to get
this flight back to London.

00:08:43.834 --> 00:08:45.667
There was
a huge family emergency.

00:08:45.667 --> 00:08:49.100
And I said to myself,
"Lord, help me if I make it

00:08:49.100 --> 00:08:51.834
to the airport, but I have to
get on this flight."

00:08:51.834 --> 00:08:54.968
And so I said to the paparazzi,
"This is so out of my character,

00:08:54.968 --> 00:08:56.133
but I have no other way
to get to the airport."

00:08:56.133 --> 00:08:57.734
-Well, you can't say
that anymore.

00:08:57.734 --> 00:08:59.133
-Now the whole world knows.

00:08:59.133 --> 00:09:00.467
"I have no other way
to get to the airport.

00:09:00.467 --> 00:09:01.968
Please, can you drive me
to the airport?"

00:09:01.968 --> 00:09:03.300
And he said,
"Jump in, let's go."

00:09:03.300 --> 00:09:04.501
-Oh, my God!
-Wow!

00:09:04.501 --> 00:09:07.667
-Thank you to that paparazzi.
Good for you.

00:09:07.667 --> 00:09:09.467
My thanks to
Derek Jeter, Rita Ora.

00:09:09.467 --> 00:09:10.467
Thank you for playing.

